      {
        "id": 175802,
        "name": "UXM266",
        "username": "UXM266",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/uxm266/{size}/1966_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-07-06T13:15:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I THINK I can confirm the following</p><p>1) Environments do not matter. I stayed in Insula Primalis for all three. That damage boost from obsidian fields was a huge help.</p><p>2) The order of heroes does not matter. As mentioned earlier, Omnitron-X can go anywhere.</p><p>3) The number of heroes is not needed. I played three heroes for all the games.&nbsp;</p><p>4) In the first game Omnitron X also gave the final blow on his turn, when \"Slip Through Time\" was played. I think i used the power that does damage based on the plating.</p><p>5) I cannot recall perfectly, but Omnitron X was incapacitated by a hero in the second game.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
